<report>
<title>Unpaired t test</title>

<p>Mean of <in>title_0</in> = <inu>mean_0</inu>  (n = <in>n0</in>)<br />
Mean of <in>title_1</in> = <inu>mean_1</inu>  (n = <in>n1</in>)</p>

<p><u>Assuming equal variances</u><br />
Combined standard error = <inu>error</inu><br />
df = <in>df</in><br />
t =  <inu>t</inu><br />
<pval>One sided <inp>p_1</inp></pval><br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2</inp></pval></p>

<p><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for difference between means = <inu>from</inu> to <inu>to</inu></ci></p>

<p>Power <in>pwr</in></p>

<p><u>Assuming unequal variances</u><br />
Combined standard error = <inu>error_unequal</inu><br />
df = <inu>df_unequal</inu><br />
t(d) =  <inu>t_unequal</inu><br />
<pval>One sided <inp>p_1_unequal</inp></pval><br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2_unequal</inp></pval></p>

<p><ci><in>pc_unequal</in>% confidence interval for difference between means = <inu>from_unequal</inu> to <inu>to_unequal</inu></ci></p>

<p>Power <in>pwr_unequal</in></p>

<p><u>Comparison of variances</u><br />
<in>say1</in><br />
<in>say2</in></p>
</report>
